IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrca-dates`
IMPORT `wrca-core`

-- Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) -- the injured worker's questions, and the dependants' on a death.
--
-- SEAT: the worker to whom the Act is applied, injured in Tasmanian employment; on the worker's death, the worker's
-- dependants. "Am I covered, and what must I do by when? What is my weekly payment now, after each step-down, and when
-- does it stop? What lump sum for my impairment? What do my dependants receive if I die?" The rules are in wrca-core.l4;
-- this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule. Its names differ from those of the
-- employer's seat (wrca-seat-employer.l4), so a case file can import both.
--
-- The basic salary is asked as a figure: it is gazetted each year (s 66) and is not in the deposited text.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act -- the worker's questions`

§§ `Am I covered, and what must I do by when?`

@export Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) (s 25, s 3)?
GIVEN `I work for my employer under a contract of service or a training contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for the employer as an employee (a contract of service, written or not) or as an apprentice or trainee under a training contract; not as an independent contractor
      `my injury is a disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is a disease (any ailment, disorder, defect or morbid condition, sudden or gradual), rather than an injury such as a fall, cut or strain
      `my injury arose out of or in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury that is not a disease: whether it arose out of, or happened in the course of, your work for this employer
      `I was hurt travelling, absent from work, or at an off-site social or sporting event, without my employer's request or authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury happened while travelling between home and work or between two employers, while temporarily away from the workplace on a working day, or at a social or sporting activity away from work, in each case not at your employer's request or direction or with its authority (s 25(6))
      `my employment was the major or most significant factor in my disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether your employment was the major or most significant factor contributing to it
      `my disease is a mental one arising mainly from reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether it is an illness or disorder of the mind arising substantially from reasonable action by your employer to transfer, demote, discipline, counsel or dismiss you, or reasonable administrative action, or a reasonable refusal of a promotion, transfer or benefit
      `my injury is attributable to my serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is attributable to your own serious and wilful misconduct
      `my injury caused death or serious and permanent incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in death or in serious and permanent incapacity
      `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you injured yourself intentionally
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
`Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` MEANS
    `the employer's liability under s 25`
        (`Liability facts` WITH
            `the person works for the employer under a contract of service or a training contract`                          IS `I work for my employer under a contract of service or a training contract`
            `the injury is a disease`                                                                                      IS `my injury is a disease`
            `the injury arose out of or in the course of the employment`                                                   IS `my injury arose out of or in the course of my employment`
            `the injury occurred in circumstances that s 25(6) says do not arise from the employment`                     IS `I was hurt travelling, absent from work, or at an off-site social or sporting event, without my employer's request or authority`
            `the employment was the major or most significant factor contributing to the disease`                         IS `my employment was the major or most significant factor in my disease`
            `the disease is an illness or disorder of the mind arising substantially from reasonable management action`  IS `my disease is a mental one arising mainly from reasonable management action`
            `the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct`                                    IS `my injury is attributable to my serious and wilful misconduct`
            `the injury resulted in the death or serious and permanent incapacity of the worker`                          IS `my injury caused death or serious and permanent incapacity`
            `the injury was intentionally self-inflicted`                                                                  IS `my injury was intentionally self-inflicted`)

GIVEN injury IS A DATE, deaf IS A BOOLEAN, employed IS A BOOLEAN, ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claim timing facts`
`my claim timing` injury deaf employed ended MEANS
    `Claim timing facts` WITH
        `the day of the injury`                           IS injury
        `the injury resulted in the death of the worker`  IS FALSE
        `the day of the death`                            IS injury   -- placeholder: no death in the worker's own claim
        `the injury is industrial deafness`               IS deaf
        `the worker is still employed by the employer`    IS employed
        `the day the employment ended`                    IS ended

@export By when must I make my claim for compensation (s 32(1)(b), (2))?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (for a disease, the day it first incapacitated you, s 3(5); for industrial deafness this date is not used)
      `my injury is industrial deafness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is permanent loss of hearing caused by exposure to industrial noise at work
      `I still work for that employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For industrial deafness: whether you still work for the employer in whose employment the deafness arose
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc For industrial deafness, if you have left: the day that employment ended (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `Claim deadline`
`By when must I make my claim` MEANS
    `the s 32 deadline for the claim` (`my claim timing` `the day of my injury` `my injury is industrial deafness` `I still work for that employer` `the day my employment ended`)

@export Is my claim for compensation in time, and if late, is it still valid (ss 32, 34(2), 38)?
GIVEN `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened (for a disease, the day it first incapacitated you)
      `my injury is industrial deafness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is permanent loss of hearing caused by exposure to industrial noise at work
      `I still work for that employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For industrial deafness: whether you still work for the employer in whose employment the deafness arose
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc For industrial deafness, if you have left: the day that employment ended (otherwise any date)
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received both the claim form and the medical certificate (a claim is not made until both are given, s 34(2))
      `I was late because my employer did not give me the right-to-claim notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lateness was occasioned by your employer's failure to tell you, within 14 days of learning of the injury, of your right to claim (s 33A, s 38(2)(aa))
      `I was late through mistake, absence from Tasmania or another reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lateness was occasioned by a mistake, your absence from the State, or another reasonable cause (such as a payment you believed was compensation, or something said on your employer's behalf about whether compensation would be paid); the Tribunal decides if this is disputed
GIVETH A `Claim time answer`
`Is my claim in time` MEANS
    `whether the claim is in time under s 32` (`my claim timing` `the day of my injury` `my injury is industrial deafness` `I still work for that employer` `the day my employment ended`) `the day I made my claim` `I was late because my employer did not give me the right-to-claim notice` `I was late through mistake, absence from Tasmania or another reasonable cause`

@export Did I give my employer notice of my injury as the Act requires (s 32(1)(a), (3), s 37)?
GIVEN `my injury is industrial deafness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is permanent loss of hearing caused by exposure to industrial noise at work (notice is not required for it)
      `I told my employer, or gave a claim, as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told your employer, your supervisor or a person authorised to receive it of the injury (orally or in writing), or gave your employer a claim, as soon as practicable after the injury
      `I did so before I chose to leave that job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did so before you voluntarily left the employment in which you were injured
      `the delay had a reasonable cause and did not prejudice my employer's defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not: whether the failure was due to a mistake, your absence from Tasmania or another reasonable cause, and your employer's defence has not been prejudiced by it (the Tribunal decides if this is disputed)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`Did I give notice of my injury as required` MEANS
    `whether notice of the injury was given under s 32(1)(a)` `my injury is industrial deafness` `I told my employer, or gave a claim, as soon as practicable` `I did so before I chose to leave that job` `the delay had a reasonable cause and did not prejudice my employer's defence`

@export By when must my employer tell me, in the prescribed form, that I may have a right to claim compensation (s 33A, reg 19, Sch 1)?
GIVEN `the day I told my employer of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day you told your employer of the injury
      `I told my employer by giving it my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first your employer learnt of the injury was your claim for compensation being served on it
GIVETH A `Right-to-claim notice answer`
`By when must my employer tell me of my right to claim` MEANS
    `the s 33A notice` `the day I told my employer of my injury` `I told my employer by giving it my claim`

@export By when must my employer or its insurer tell me in writing whether it accepts liability for my claim (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day my employer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim for compensation
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I be told whether my claim is accepted` MEANS
    `the s 39 deadline for the status notice` `the day my employer received my claim`

@export By when must my employer start my weekly payments (s 81(1))?
GIVEN `the day my employer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim for compensation
      `my first pay day after that` IS A DATE @desc The first day after your employer received the claim on which you would normally be paid your wages
      `it is reasonably practicable for my employer to start on that pay day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If that pay day is within 14 days of the claim: whether it is reasonably practicable for your employer to start payments on it
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my weekly payments start` MEANS
    `the s 81 deadline to commence weekly payments` `the day my employer received my claim` `my first pay day after that` `it is reasonably practicable for my employer to start on that pay day`

@export From what date are my weekly payments payable (s 81(3))?
GIVEN `the day my incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became unable to work, wholly or partly, because of the injury
      `the day I gave my claim to my employer` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your claim for compensation (with its medical certificate) to your employer
GIVETH A DATE
`From what date are my weekly payments payable` MEANS
    `the day weekly payments are payable from under s 81(3)` `the day my incapacity began` `the day I gave my claim to my employer`

@export Has my employer disputed my claim in time, or is it taken to have accepted liability (ss 81A, 81AB)?
GIVEN `the day my employer received my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim for compensation
      `my employer has served me a written dispute notice with reasons and referred it to the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has done all three: served you written notice that it disputes liability, told you its reasons, and referred the matter to the Tribunal
      `the day it did the last of those` IS A DATE @desc If it has: the day it completed the last of those three steps (otherwise any date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
`Is my employer taken to have accepted liability for my claim` MEANS
    `whether liability is taken to have been accepted under s 81AB` `the day my employer received my claim` `my employer has served me a written dispute notice with reasons and referred it to the Tribunal` `the day it did the last of those` `today`

§§ `What is my weekly payment, how does it step down, and when does it stop?`

GIVEN start IS A DATE, began IS A DATE, paid IS A NUMBER, ot IS A NUMBER, req IS A BOOLEAN, rost IS A BOOLEAN, unif IS A BOOLEAN, cont IS A BOOLEAN
      bonus IS A NUMBER, allow IS A NUMBER, two IS A BOOLEAN, others IS A NUMBER, ft IS A `Full-time contract`, comp IS A BOOLEAN, cnwe IS A NUMBER, rate IS A NUMBER, hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earnings facts`
`my earnings` start began paid ot req rost unif cont bonus allow two others ft comp cnwe rate hours MEANS
    `Earnings facts` WITH
        `the day the incapacity began`                                                                      IS began
        `the day continuous employment with the employer began`                                             IS start
        `everything the employer paid for work in the relevant period`                                      IS paid
        `the part of it paid for overtime or excess hours`                                                  IS ot
        `overtime`                                                                                          IS `Overtime facts` WITH
                                                                                                                `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS req
                                                                                                                `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS rost
                                                                                                                `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS unif
                                                                                                                `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS cont
        `the part of it paid at the employer's discretion as a bonus, gratuity or similar payment`          IS bonus
        `the part of it paid for special expenses of the employment or as travel, meal or accommodation allowances` IS allow
        `the worker had contracts of service with 2 or more employers when the incapacity began`            IS two
        `the average weekly earnings in the other employments, added together`                              IS others
        `which contract is full-time`                                                                       IS ft
        `there is another worker of the employer doing comparable work`                                     IS comp
        `that worker's normal weekly earnings`                                                              IS cnwe
        `the hourly rate of pay, without overtime or shift or other allowances`                             IS rate
        `the hours a week the worker agreed or was rostered to work in the pay period of the incapacity`    IS hours

@export What are my normal weekly earnings for workers compensation (ss 69(2), (2A), (14), 70(2))?
GIVEN `the day my employment with this employer began` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous employment with this employer began
      `the day my incapacity began` IS A DATE @desc The day you first became unable to work, wholly or partly, because of the injury
      `all I was paid for work in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc Everything this employer paid you for work in the 12 months before the incapacity (or since you started, if less than 12 months), in dollars, including overtime, bonuses and allowances
      `the overtime part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that was for overtime or hours beyond your minimum guaranteed contracted hours, in dollars
      `my overtime was required by my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether working overtime or excess hours was a requirement of your contract of employment
      `my overtime was regular and rostered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you worked it in a regular and established pattern, in accordance with a roster
      `my overtime was the same number of hours each time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pattern was substantially uniform in the number of overtime hours
      `I would have kept working that overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have kept working overtime in that pattern if you had not been injured
      `the discretionary bonus part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid at your employer's discretion as a bonus, gratuity or similar payment, in dollars (left out)
      `the allowances part` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid to cover special expenses of the job, or as travel, meal or accommodation allowances, in dollars (left out)
      `I had more than one employer when the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had contracts of service with two or more employers when the incapacity began
      `my average weekly earnings from my other jobs` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: your average weekly earnings in your other jobs, added together, in dollars (0 if none)
      `which of my jobs is full-time` IS A `Full-time contract` @desc If you had more than one employer: which contract, if any, is full-time (for another employer's, give your average weekly earnings in it)
      `another worker of my employer does comparable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you had worked for this employer 14 days or less: whether another worker of the same employer does comparable work
      `that worker's normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: that worker's normal weekly earnings, in dollars (otherwise 0)
      `my hourly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc If you had worked for this employer 14 days or less: your hourly rate under your contract or award, without overtime or shift or other allowances, in dollars
      `my agreed or rostered hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If you had worked for this employer 14 days or less: the hours a week you agreed, or were rostered, to work in the pay period of the incapacity
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my normal weekly earnings` MEANS
    `the normal weekly earnings` (`my earnings` `the day my employment with this employer began` `the day my incapacity began` `all I was paid for work in the relevant period` `the overtime part` `my overtime was required by my contract` `my overtime was regular and rostered` `my overtime was the same number of hours each time` `I would have kept working that overtime` `the discretionary bonus part` `the allowances part` `I had more than one employer when the incapacity began` `my average weekly earnings from my other jobs` `which of my jobs is full-time` `another worker of my employer does comparable work` `that worker's normal weekly earnings` `my hourly rate of pay` `my agreed or rostered hours a week`)

@export What is my weekly payment before any step-down (s 69(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly earnings (see "What are my normal weekly earnings"), in dollars
      `a doctor has certified my incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your incapacity is supported by a certificate in the approved form signed by a medical practitioner or accredited person
      `I am totally unable to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are totally incapacitated for work (otherwise partly)
      `my ordinary hourly rate before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary-time hourly rate of pay for the work you did immediately before the incapacity, in dollars
      `my ordinary hours a week before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The ordinary hours a week you were engaged for immediately before the incapacity
      `the rise in my ordinary hourly rate since then` IS A NUMBER @desc How much your ordinary hourly rate for that work has risen (or, as a negative number, fallen) since the incapacity began, under your contract or award, in dollars (0 if unchanged)
      `what I earn or could earn a week in suitable work` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are partly incapacitated: what you are earning, or would be able to earn, a week in suitable employment or business, in dollars (0 if totally incapacitated)
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`What is my weekly payment before any step-down` MEANS
    `the weekly payment under s 69 for normal weekly earnings of` `my normal weekly earnings`
        (`Incapacity facts` WITH
            `the incapacity is supported by a certificate in the approved form`                                   IS `a doctor has certified my incapacity`
            `the incapacity is total`                                                                             IS `I am totally unable to work`
            `the ordinary hourly rate of pay immediately before the incapacity`                                   IS `my ordinary hourly rate before the incapacity`
            `the ordinary hours a week the worker was engaged for immediately before the incapacity`             IS `my ordinary hours a week before the incapacity`
            `the change in the ordinary hourly rate under the contract or industrial instrument since then`       IS `the rise in my ordinary hourly rate since then`
            `what the worker is earning or could earn a week in suitable employment or business`                  IS `what I earn or could earn a week in suitable work`)

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, pension IS A NUMBER, injury IS A DATE, initial IS A DATE, assessed IS A BOOLEAN, wpi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cessation facts`
`my cessation facts` dob pension injury initial assessed wpi MEANS
    `Cessation facts` WITH
        `the worker's date of birth`                         IS dob
        `the worker's pension age in years`                  IS pension
        `the day of the injury`                              IS injury
        `the day of the initial incapacity`                  IS initial
        `the permanent impairment has been assessed`         IS assessed
        `the whole person impairment, as a percentage`       IS wpi

@export On what date does my entitlement to weekly payments stop (s 69B(1)(c), (2E), s 87)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `my pension age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), in years (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened
      `the day my incapacity first began` IS A DATE @desc The day you were first incapacitated by the injury (the date of the initial incapacity)
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permanent impairment has been assessed as a percentage of the whole person
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc If assessed: the percentage of whole person impairment (for example 16 for 16%)
GIVETH A `Cessation answer`
`When does my entitlement to weekly payments stop` MEANS
    `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`my cessation facts` `my date of birth` `my pension age` `the day of my injury` `the day my incapacity first began` `my impairment has been assessed` `my whole person impairment`)

-- The step-down days, for an incapacity without a break.
DECLARE `My step-down days` HAS
    `the first day at 90% (or 95%)`                                                                      IS A DATE
    `the first day at 80% (or 85%)`                                                                      IS A DATE

@export On what dates does my weekly payment step down, if my incapacity continues without a break (s 69B(1), (6))?
GIVEN `the day my incapacity first began` IS A DATE @desc The day you were first incapacitated by the injury (the date of the initial incapacity)
GIVETH A `My step-down days`
`When does my weekly payment step down` MEANS
    `My step-down days` WITH
        `the first day at 90% (or 95%)` IS `the first day of week 27 after an initial incapacity on` `the day my incapacity first began`
        `the first day at 80% (or 85%)` IS `the first day of week 79 after an initial incapacity on` `the day my incapacity first began`

GIVEN parttime IS A BOOLEAN, engaged IS A NUMBER, fulltime IS A NUMBER, bs IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Floor facts`
`my floor facts` parttime engaged fulltime bs MEANS
    `Floor facts` WITH
        `the basic salary`                                                                                   IS bs
        `the worker was working part-time or casually at the time of the injury`                             IS parttime
        `the hours a week the worker was engaged for immediately before the incapacity`                      IS engaged
        `the hours a week of full-time employment`                                                           IS fulltime

@export What weekly payment do I get for a given week of my incapacity, after any step-down and with the minimum (s 69B)?
GIVEN `my weekly payment before any step-down` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment under s 69 (see "What is my weekly payment before any step-down"), in dollars
      `the number of this week in my incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of your incapacity this is, counting every week of incapacity from this injury together (1 for the first week)
      `the first day of this week` IS A DATE @desc The date this week begins
      `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is medical evidence that you cannot perform your usual duties with your employer this week
      `a doctor says I can do suitable alternative duties with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is medical evidence that you can return to suitable alternative duties with your employer this week
      `my employer does not let me do suitable alternative duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer does not enable you to undertake suitable alternative duties this week
      `the hours I work this week under an approved return-to-work or injury management plan` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you work this week under your approved return-to-work plan or approved injury management plan (0 if none)
      `what I earn this week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn from work this week, in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `I worked for my employer more than 14 days before the incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been employed by this employer for more than 14 days before you were first incapacitated
      `my average ordinary hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc If more than 14 days: the average ordinary hours a week you were employed for, without overtime
      `the hours a week I agreed to work` IS A NUMBER @desc If 14 days or less: the hours a week you agreed to work in the pay period when the incapacity arose, without overtime
      `the hours a week I was rostered` IS A NUMBER @desc If 14 days or less: the hours a week you were rostered in that pay period, without overtime
      `my average overtime hours a week` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average overtime or excess hours a week (0 if none)
      `my overtime was required by my contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether working overtime was a requirement of your contract of employment
      `my overtime was regular and rostered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you worked it in a regular and established pattern, in accordance with a roster
      `my overtime was the same number of hours each time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pattern was substantially uniform in the number of overtime hours
      `I would have kept working that overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have kept working overtime in that pattern if not injured
      `I was part-time or casual when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were working part-time or casually at the time of the injury
      `the hours a week I worked just before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you were engaged for immediately before the incapacity
      `the hours of a full-time week in my work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week of full-time employment in your work (for example 38)
      `this year's basic salary` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary for this year as gazetted under s 66, in dollars a week (not in the deposited law: ask WorkSafe Tasmania)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `my pension age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), in years (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened
      `the day my incapacity first began` IS A DATE @desc The day you were first incapacitated by the injury
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permanent impairment has been assessed as a percentage of the whole person
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc If assessed: the percentage of whole person impairment
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`What is my weekly payment for this week` MEANS
    `the weekly payment for the week under s 69B`
        (`a weekly payment of` `my weekly payment before any step-down`)
        (`Week facts` WITH
            `the week of the period of incapacity`                                                               IS `the number of this week in my incapacity`
            `the first day of the week`                                                                          IS `the first day of this week`
            `there is medical evidence the worker cannot perform the usual duties with the employer`             IS `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties with my employer`
            `there is medical evidence the worker can return to suitable alternative duties with the employer`   IS `a doctor says I can do suitable alternative duties with my employer`
            `the employer does not enable the worker to undertake suitable alternative duties`                   IS `my employer does not let me do suitable alternative duties`
            `the hours worked in the week under an approved return-to-work or injury management plan`            IS `the hours I work this week under an approved return-to-work or injury management plan`
            `the worker's earnings in the week`                                                                  IS `what I earn this week`)
        (`Normal hours facts` WITH
            `the worker was employed by the employer for more than 14 days before the initial incapacity`        IS `I worked for my employer more than 14 days before the incapacity`
            `the average ordinary hours a week the worker was employed for`                                      IS `my average ordinary hours a week`
            `the hours a week the worker agreed to work in the pay period of the incapacity`                     IS `the hours a week I agreed to work`
            `the hours a week the worker was rostered to work in that pay period`                                IS `the hours a week I was rostered`
            `the average overtime or excess hours a week`                                                        IS `my average overtime hours a week`
            `overtime`                                                                                           IS `Overtime facts` WITH
                `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS `my overtime was required by my contract`
                `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS `my overtime was regular and rostered`
                `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS `my overtime was the same number of hours each time`
                `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS `I would have kept working that overtime`)
        (`my floor facts` `I was part-time or casual when injured` `the hours a week I worked just before the incapacity` `the hours of a full-time week in my work` `this year's basic salary`)
        (`the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`my cessation facts` `my date of birth` `my pension age` `the day of my injury` `the day my incapacity first began` `my impairment has been assessed` `my whole person impairment`))

-- The schedule: what is paid in each band, for an incapacity without a break, the same s 69B(2) position throughout, no
-- work under a plan, and the same earnings each week.
DECLARE `My weekly payment schedule` HAS
    `in the first 26 weeks`                                                                              IS A `Weekly payment answer`
    `from week 27 to week 78`                                                                            IS A `Weekly payment answer`
    `after week 78`                                                                                      IS A `Weekly payment answer`
    `the first day at 90% (or 95%)`                                                                      IS A DATE
    `the first day at 80% (or 85%)`                                                                      IS A DATE
    `when the payments stop`                                                                             IS A `Cessation answer`

@export What will I be paid each week now, after each step-down, and until when, if my incapacity continues without a break (ss 69B, 87)?
GIVEN `my weekly payment before any step-down` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly payment under s 69 (see "What is my weekly payment before any step-down"), in dollars
      `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties, can do suitable duties, and my employer does not offer them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, throughout, there is medical evidence that you cannot do your usual duties but can do suitable alternative duties with your employer, and your employer does not enable you to do them (s 69B(2): 95% and 85% instead of 90% and 80%)
      `what I earn a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What you earn from work each week, in dollars (0 if nothing)
      `I was part-time or casual when injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were working part-time or casually at the time of the injury
      `the hours a week I worked just before the incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week you were engaged for immediately before the incapacity
      `the hours of a full-time week in my work` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours a week of full-time employment in your work (for example 38)
      `this year's basic salary` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary for this year as gazetted under s 66, in dollars a week (not in the deposited law: ask WorkSafe Tasmania)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `my pension age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age pension age under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), in years (67 for anyone born on or after 1 January 1957)
      `the day of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The day the injury happened
      `the day my incapacity first began` IS A DATE @desc The day you were first incapacitated by the injury
      `my impairment has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your permanent impairment has been assessed as a percentage of the whole person
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc If assessed: the percentage of whole person impairment
GIVETH A `My weekly payment schedule`
`What will I be paid each week and until when` MEANS
    `My weekly payment schedule` WITH
        `in the first 26 weeks`           IS `the payment in week` 1 `the day my incapacity first began`
        `from week 27 to week 78`         IS `the payment in week` 27 `week 27 begins`
        `after week 78`                   IS `the payment in week` 79 `week 79 begins`
        `the first day at 90% (or 95%)`   IS `week 27 begins`
        `the first day at 80% (or 85%)`   IS `week 79 begins`
        `when the payments stop`          IS `the cessation`
    WHERE
        `week 27 begins` MEANS `the first day of week 27 after an initial incapacity on` `the day my incapacity first began`
        `week 79 begins` MEANS `the first day of week 79 after an initial incapacity on` `the day my incapacity first began`
        `the cessation`  MEANS `the day the entitlement to weekly payments ceases` (`my cessation facts` `my date of birth` `my pension age` `the day of my injury` `the day my incapacity first began` `my impairment has been assessed` `my whole person impairment`)
        GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, first IS A DATE
        GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
        `the payment in week` n first MEANS
            `the weekly payment for the week under s 69B`
                (`a weekly payment of` `my weekly payment before any step-down`)
                (`Week facts` WITH
                    `the week of the period of incapacity`                                                               IS n
                    `the first day of the week`                                                                          IS first
                    `there is medical evidence the worker cannot perform the usual duties with the employer`             IS `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties, can do suitable duties, and my employer does not offer them`
                    `there is medical evidence the worker can return to suitable alternative duties with the employer`   IS `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties, can do suitable duties, and my employer does not offer them`
                    `the employer does not enable the worker to undertake suitable alternative duties`                   IS `a doctor says I cannot do my usual duties, can do suitable duties, and my employer does not offer them`
                    `the hours worked in the week under an approved return-to-work or injury management plan`            IS 0
                    `the worker's earnings in the week`                                                                  IS `what I earn a week`)
                -- placeholder: with no work under a plan, s 69B(2A) is never met, so the normal hours are not read
                (`Normal hours facts` WITH
                    `the worker was employed by the employer for more than 14 days before the initial incapacity`        IS TRUE
                    `the average ordinary hours a week the worker was employed for`                                      IS 1
                    `the hours a week the worker agreed to work in the pay period of the incapacity`                     IS 0
                    `the hours a week the worker was rostered to work in that pay period`                                IS 0
                    `the average overtime or excess hours a week`                                                        IS 0
                    `overtime`                                                                                           IS `Overtime facts` WITH
                        `the overtime or excess hours were a requirement of the contract of employment`       IS FALSE
                        `they were worked in a regular and established pattern and in accordance with a roster` IS FALSE
                        `the pattern was substantially uniform as to the number of hours`                     IS FALSE
                        `the worker would have continued to work them in that pattern if not incapacitated`   IS FALSE)
                (`my floor facts` `I was part-time or casual when injured` `the hours a week I worked just before the incapacity` `the hours of a full-time week in my work` `this year's basic salary`)
                `the cessation`

§§ `What lump sum is payable for my permanent impairment?`

@export What lump sum is payable for my permanent impairment (s 71)? The answer is 0 below the threshold
GIVEN `the kind of impairment` IS AN `Impairment kind` @desc The kind of permanent impairment: a physical impairment, a physical impairment that is the loss of part or all of a finger or toe, or a psychiatric impairment (an illness or disorder of the mind)
      `my whole person impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage of whole person impairment assessed by an accredited medical practitioner (for example 12 for 12%)
      `I lost a pregnancy of at least 16 weeks through the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in the loss of a foetus you had carried for at least 16 weeks since conception (counted as a further 20%)
      `the basic salary for the year of my injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary gazetted under s 66 for the calendar year in which the injury happened, in dollars (the lump sum is calculated as at the date of the injury)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What lump sum is payable for my impairment` MEANS
    `the s 71 lump sum` `the kind of impairment` `my whole person impairment` `I lost a pregnancy of at least 16 weeks through the injury` `the basic salary for the year of my injury`

@export What whole person impairment does my binaural hearing impairment convert to (s 73(4), reg 20)?
GIVEN `my binaural hearing impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your binaural hearing impairment from industrial deafness, as a percentage, as determined by a qualified person under the NAL tables (s 73(3), reg 20(2)), leaving out loss from other causes, from outside Tasmania or already compensated
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What whole person impairment is my hearing loss` MEANS
    `the reg 20 whole person impairment for a binaural hearing impairment of` `my binaural hearing impairment`

@export What lump sum is payable for my industrial deafness (ss 72A, 73, 71(1), reg 20)? The answer is 0 at 5% binaural hearing impairment or less
GIVEN `my binaural hearing impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your binaural hearing impairment from industrial deafness, as a percentage, as determined under the NAL tables, leaving out loss from other causes, from outside Tasmania or already compensated
      `the basic salary for the year of my injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary gazetted under s 66 for the year of the date of injury (for deafness: the last day of that employment, or the day of the claim if still employed, s 73A), in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What lump sum is payable for my industrial deafness` MEANS
    `the industrial deafness lump sum for a binaural hearing impairment of` `my binaural hearing impairment` `at a basic salary of` `the basic salary for the year of my injury`

§§ `If the worker dies: what do the dependants receive?`
-- Situation: only after the worker's death from the injury. Asked by a dependant.

@export By when must a claim be made after the worker's death from the injury (s 32(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the worker was injured` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker was injured
      `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died as a result of the injury
GIVETH A `Claim deadline`
`By when must the dependants claim` MEANS
    `the s 32 deadline for the claim`
        (`Claim timing facts` WITH
            `the day of the injury`                           IS `the day the worker was injured`
            `the injury resulted in the death of the worker`  IS TRUE
            `the day of the death`                            IS `the day the worker died`
            `the injury is industrial deafness`               IS FALSE
            `the worker is still employed by the employer`    IS FALSE   -- placeholder: not read for a death claim
            `the day the employment ended`                    IS `the day the worker died`)   -- placeholder: not read for a death claim

@export What lump sum is payable on the worker's death, and to whom (s 67)?
GIVEN `the spouse or caring partner was` IS A `Dependency` @desc Whether the worker's spouse (including a partner in a significant relationship) or registered caring partner was wholly dependent, partially dependent or not dependent on the worker's earnings (not dependent if there is none)
      `the number of wholly dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children (under 16, or 16 to 20 and studying full time) were wholly dependent on the worker
      `the number of partially dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children were partially dependent on the worker
      `of those, the children who are not the spouse's or caring partner's` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those dependent children are not children of the spouse or caring partner
      `the number of other dependent family members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other members of the worker's family (parents, grandparents, brothers, sisters and so on) were dependent on the worker
      `the worker was helping to maintain the family home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with no dependants, the worker was contributing to the maintenance of the home of members of the family just before the death
      `this year's basic salary` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary for this year as gazetted under s 66, in dollars a week
GIVETH A `Death lump sum answer`
`What lump sum is payable on the worker's death` MEANS
    `the s 67 lump sum`
        (`Death facts` WITH
            `the spouse or caring partner`                                                                       IS `the spouse or caring partner was`
            `wholly dependent children`                                                                          IS `the number of wholly dependent children`
            `partially dependent children`                                                                       IS `the number of partially dependent children`
            `of those, the children who are not children of the spouse or caring partner`                        IS `of those, the children who are not the spouse's or caring partner's`
            `other dependants`                                                                                   IS `the number of other dependent family members`
            `the worker was contributing to the maintenance of the home of members of the family`                IS `the worker was helping to maintain the family home`)
        `this year's basic salary`

GIVEN death IS A DATE, claim IS A DATE, rate IS A NUMBER, long IS A BOOLEAN, claims IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouse weekly facts`
`the spouse's facts` death claim rate long claims MEANS
    `Spouse weekly facts` WITH
        `the day of the death`                                                                               IS death
        `the day the claim was given to the employer`                                                        IS claim
        `the weekly payment the worker would have had for total incapacity`                                  IS rate
        `the worker died more than 78 weeks after the injury, while receiving compensation for it`           IS long
        `the number of claims for these weekly payments`                                                     IS claims

@export From what date are weekly payments to the worker's dependent spouse or caring partner payable (s 67A(1)(a), s 67B(3))?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died as a result of the injury
      `the day the dependant's claim was given to the employer` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim for these weekly payments was given to the employer
GIVETH A DATE
`From what date are the spouse's weekly payments payable` MEANS
    -- placeholder rate, claim count and duration: the payable-from date does not read them
    `the day the spouse's weekly payments are payable from` (`the spouse's facts` `the day the worker died` `the day the dependant's claim was given to the employer` 0 FALSE 1)

@export What weekly payment does the worker's dependent spouse or caring partner receive on a given day (s 67A(1)(a), (2)-(4), s 67B)?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died as a result of the injury
      `the day the dependant's claim was given to the employer` IS A DATE @desc The day the claim for these weekly payments was given to the employer
      `the worker's weekly payment for total incapacity` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payment the worker would have received if totally incapacitated (s 69(1)(a): the greater of normal weekly earnings and the ordinary-time weekly rate), in dollars
      `the worker died more than 78 weeks after the injury while receiving compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died more than 78 weeks after the injury, while receiving compensation for it
      `the number of claims for these payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many claims have been made for these weekly payments (they are divided equally; 1 if only yours)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the weekly rate
GIVETH A `Dependant weekly answer`
`What weekly payment does the dependent spouse receive` MEANS
    `the s 67A weekly rate payable to the spouse or caring partner on` (`the spouse's facts` `the day the worker died` `the day the dependant's claim was given to the employer` `the worker's weekly payment for total incapacity` `the worker died more than 78 weeks after the injury while receiving compensation` `the number of claims for these payments`) `the day in question`

@export What weekly payment does a dependent child of the worker receive on a given day (s 67A(1)(b), s 65)?
GIVEN `the day the worker died` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker died as a result of the injury
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the weekly rate
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The child's date of birth
      `the child is a full-time student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student on that day (counts from 16 to 20)
      `the child was dependent on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was wholly or partly dependent on the worker's earnings
      `this year's basic salary` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic salary for this year as gazetted under s 66, in dollars a week
GIVETH A `Dependant weekly answer`
`What weekly payment does a dependent child receive` MEANS
    `the s 67A weekly rate payable to a dependent child` `the day the worker died` `the day in question` `this year's basic salary`
        (`the child was dependent on the worker` AND (`a person aged` (`the age in whole years of a person born on` `the child's date of birth` `on` `the day in question`) `is a child under s 65, being a full-time student or not` `the child is a full-time student`))

@export How much is paid toward the worker's burial or cremation (s 75(1)(b)(i), reg 21(1))?
GIVEN `the reasonable cost of the burial or cremation` IS A NUMBER @desc The reasonable expenses of the worker's burial or cremation, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is paid toward the funeral` MEANS
    `the s 75(1)(b)(i) amount for burial or cremation expenses of` `the reasonable cost of the burial or cremation`

@export How much is paid toward counselling for the worker's family (s 75(1)(b)(ii), reg 21(2))?
GIVEN `the reasonable cost of counselling for the family` IS A NUMBER @desc The reasonable costs of counselling services (by medical practitioners, registered psychologists, social workers or recognised counsellors) for members of the family, in total, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is paid toward family counselling` MEANS
    `the s 75(1)(b)(ii) amount for counselling costs of` `the reasonable cost of counselling for the family`

§§ `Travelling expenses`

@export How much of my travel to treatment or a required medical examination is paid (s 76, reg 22)?
GIVEN `my reasonable fares, meals and accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc Your reasonable travel and maintenance expenses other than driving a private car, for treatment or a required medical examination, in dollars
      `the kilometres I drove my own car` IS A NUMBER @desc The kilometres you drove a private car for those purposes
      `the State Service Award rate per kilometre` IS A NUMBER @desc The occasional-user private vehicle rate per kilometre in the Tasmanian State Service Award, in dollars (not in the deposited law)
      `the amount prescribed by reg 22` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount for the travel at the same rate and on the same terms as the Award's equivalent travelling expenses, in dollars (not in the deposited law)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my travel is paid` MEANS
    `the s 76(1) travelling compensation` `my reasonable fares, meals and accommodation` `the kilometres I drove my own car` `the State Service Award rate per kilometre` `the amount prescribed by reg 22`
